<section id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Effect sizes and per-seed wins.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Cohen’s <math id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> values relative to LN backbone are in Table <a href="#A4.T16" title="Table A16 ‣ Effect sizes and per-seed wins. ‣ D.7 Equivalence and ablations ‣ Appendix D Empirical Appendix ‣ PostDeg: Placement Beats Parameterization in LayerNorm GNNs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A16</span></a>. The values for PostDeg and its learned variants exceed <math id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math> on three tasks because between-seed variance is unusually low at our seed budget, not because the absolute reward gap is exceptional; the per-seed reward gap in Table <a href="#A4.T12" title="Table A12 ‣ D.6 Full numerical results ‣ Appendix D Empirical Appendix ‣ PostDeg: Placement Beats Parameterization in LayerNorm GNNs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A12</span></a> is the more interpretable quantity.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T16" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A4.T16.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table A16</span>: </span><span id="A4.T16.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Cohen’s <math id="A4.T16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> against LN backbone at the largest evaluation size. Positive values favor the method (sign-flipped for lower-is-better tasks). Source: <span id="A4.T16.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">eval_results_all.csv</span>, <span id="A4.T16.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">new_experiments_eval_results.csv</span>.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A4.T16.7" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
