<div id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The win-rate table reads as paired evidence for the same claim: on each of the three degree-sensitive node-selection tasks, PostDeg and its learned variants each win on <math id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> paired seeds against LN backbone, and on the boundary task (Epidemic) wins on <math id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math>. Figure <a href="#A4.F9" title="Figure A9 ‣ Effect sizes and per-seed wins. ‣ D.7 Equivalence and ablations ‣ Appendix D Empirical Appendix ‣ PostDeg: Placement Beats Parameterization in LayerNorm GNNs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A9</span></a> renders the Cohen’s <math id="A4.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> matrix as a heatmap so the (method, task) sign and magnitude can be read at a glance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T17" class="ltx_table">
